  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "Dissolve ingredients of solution A, adjust pH to 6.2 – 6.3 and sparge with 100% N2 gas atmosphere to make it anoxic. Then distribute medium under the same gas atmosphere into anoxic Hungate-type tubes or serum vials and autoclave. Solutions B and C are prepared under 100% N2 gas atmosphere and autoclaved. Solution D is prepared under 80% N2 and 20% CO2 gas atmosphere and autoclaved. To complete the medium appropriate amounts of solutions B to D are added to the sterile solution A in the sequence as indicated. Final pH ofthe medium should be at 7.4."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": "Rumen fluid from cow or sheep (obtained from fistulated animals or abattoir refuse) is filtered through muslin, autoclaved at 121°C for 15 min and then centrifuged at 27,000 g for 20 min. The supernatant is madeanoxic by sparging with 100% N2 gas for 15 min, dispensed under same gas atmosphere into anoxic serum vials to 30% of volume and then stored frozen at -20°C."
    }
  ]
}